experiment: f3comp
  the question      §47. Given a creature with THREE audible axes, is it
                    better to SPREAD a vocabulary across them or STRETCH
                    it over two? 2x2x2 (8 words) vs 3x3 (9 words).
  matched           word count, index load, physics (one genome, f3 ON in
                    BOTH arms) and scorer (the same three-formant joint
                    error; the 3x3's nine words all carry f3 at rest).
  the primary       delivered |dF1| between the LOWEST and HIGHEST F1
                    target -- both arms ask 118.0 Hz there, so it is one
                    asked against one delivered. NOT ctxgrid's sp1, which
                    averages over all pairs and so depends on grid shape.
  render_f3_gain    1.00
  context_source    4

  instrument        f3comp   trial seed 000000000135db8e   36 creatures
                    another probe is another trial sequence: its numbers
                    are not comparable with these (~0.05 at 300 trials)

